%U A088651 53792264108455702830,43263866546732976414270,1834211334301046929508280,152058443198637095680139580
%N A088651 a(n) = smallest number k such that r*k-1 is prime for all r = 1 to n.
%C A088651 Is the sequence finite?
%H A088651 Jacob Glickman, <a href="https://github.com/jhg023/first-knowns">first-knowns: exhaustive search for A088651</a>, GitHub, 2026.
%H A088651 Carlos Rivera, <a href="https://www.primepuzzles.net/puzzles/puzz_379.htm">Puzzle 379. SG primes and its prime average</a>, The Prime Puzzles & Problems Connection.
%e A088651 a(5) = 6 because 1*6-1, 2*6-1, 3*6-1, 4*6-1, 5*6-1 are all prime.
%e A088651 a(11) = 9448481062020 because all eleven numbers 1*9448481062020-1, 2*9448481062020-1,3*9448481062020-1,...,10*9448481062020-1 & 11*9448481062020-1 are prime and 9448481062020 is the smallest number with such property.
